DISCLAIMER - kdash is provided as is, without warranty of any kind. The
person running this utility is solely responsible for its use, for having
authorisation to access the clusters and namespaces it reads, and for any
decision or action taken on its output. kdash only reads the cluster unless
interactive mode is enabled explicitly (--allow-interactive), which adds a
shell inside a container and file copy in or out of one: those two run in the
user's name with the user's rights and are NOT read-only. Every run is
AUDITED: the user, host, origin, context, namespace, every action taken in
the dashboard, every report written, every kubectl call and every interactive
attachment are logged and stored (local audit log, central audit log when
configured, and syslog).

